# Tech stack

This is a Node.js web app built with TypeScript and Next.js.

- Runtime: Node.js
- Language: TypeScript (strict). Do not add plain JavaScript source files.
- Framework: Next.js (App Router)
- UI: React with TypeScript (`.tsx`)
- Styling: CSS. Prefer colocated styles or a single global stylesheet until a styling library is chosen.
- Package manager: npm

## Conventions

- Use the App Router under `app/`. Put route handlers in `app/api/`.
- Type props, function arguments, and API request/response shapes. Avoid `any`.
- Keep server-only logic in Server Components or Route Handlers. Mark client components with `"use client"` only when they need browser APIs or interactivity.
- Use `next/link` and `next/navigation` for routing. Use `next/image` for images.
- Name files in kebab-case. Name React components in PascalCase.
